  "anand": [
    "Anand weddings booked from our Vadodara base are usually planned as a single travelling assignment rather than a standard local visit, so venue and season details matter more than they would for an in-town booking. Resort and destination-style venues around Anand often have their own preparation spaces, which we confirm with the property directly where possible, and lawn or outdoor venues need a weather-aware backup plan for the styling area. Peak wedding season brings more competing bookings across the wider Vadodara region, so Anand dates during busy weeks should be confirmed with more lead time than an off-season date would need. Because the team is travelling specifically for the Anand booking, we also factor in road or transfer time when planning the arrival buffer — an earlier ceremony time generally means an earlier departure from Vadodara. If the venue is unfamiliar to us, sharing photos or a location pin in advance helps us plan the right team size and equipment before the day itself, rather than adjusting on arrival.",
    "For a travelling Anand booking, the right package depends on guest count just as it would locally, but travel adds one more variable worth planning around: how many functions the team needs to cover during the trip. A single-ceremony booking is the most straightforward — one date, one venue, one styling window. A multi-function Anand trip, covering a haldi or sangeet alongside the main wedding, is usually more efficient as one combined package rather than separate bookings, since the team is already travelling from Vadodara and can plan artist time across the full stay. Fabric and accessory choices work the same way they would for a local booking — a coordinated palette for the groom and family, reviewed against outfit references before the team departs. Because Anand bookings involve travel, we recommend finalising the package a little earlier than you might for an in-town wedding, so fabric, artist numbers and the travel schedule can all be confirmed together rather than adjusted at short notice.",
  ],
